  "summary_en": "Nigeria's September 2025 National AI Strategy sets a vision of global AI leadership through ethical, inclusive innovation. It defines five pillars and 34 strategies covering infrastructure, ecosystem, sector adoption, responsible AI and governance, including an AI ethics expert group, a regulatory body, and risk mitigation. Robotics appears only in passing.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Five pillars with 34 strategies over a five-year implementation horizon",
   "Establish an AI Ethics Expert Group (AIEEG) to advise on ethical AI development and deployment",
   "Create an AI Governance Regulatory Body and national AI principles",
   "Develop a comprehensive AI risk management framework and standardised ethical assessment tool",
   "Data governance aligned with the Nigeria Data Protection Act, plus AI skills and compute investment"
